<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<topic id="adf89252-faed-4c5c-b4dc-6321223e6da3" revisionNumber="1">
  <developerHowToDocument
    xmlns="http://ddue.schemas.microsoft.com/authoring/2003/5"
    xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">

    <introduction>
      <para><legacyBold>Note:</legacyBold> this section and related methods are deprecated. Loading (and writing) scheduler configuration from separate files
                is now supported using standard .NET configuration files. See the <link xlink:href="85482458-faf3-4de0-95c0-ef0b3709a1ea" /> section for details.
            
            <para/>
            <para/>
                Schedulers can be configured using standalone XML files containing one or more schedule
                elements.
                <para/>
                <legacyBold>Note:</legacyBold>&#160;only the <link xlink:href="c7ca10b4-86cf-4f36-a961-826165893353">schedule</link> element is supported in standalone XML files.
               <para/> 
               <para/> 
            Here is a sample XML configuration file, schedulerconfiguration.xml:</para>
    </introduction>

    
               

<section>
  <content>
      
<code language="xml">
&lt;?xml version=&quot;1.0&quot; encoding=&quot;utf-16&quot;?&gt;
&lt;schedules&gt;
    &lt;schedule name="schedule1" type=&quot;...&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;schedule name="schedule2" type=&quot;...&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;schedule name="schedule3" type=&quot;...&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/schedules&gt;
</code>
<para/>
            The following code will load the configuration and return an initialized scheduler. 
<code language="c#">
using (Scheduler scheduler = SchedulerFactory.CreateFromXml("schedulerconfiguration.xml", "/schedules"))
{
    // ... start scheduler processing
}
</code>
</content>
</section>


    <relatedTopics>
